All 16 canonical entries are defining equations for declared proof-local functions. The only `simplification` rules are the two disjoint, exhaustive cases of `nextBalance`; they define that function rather than assert an extra arithmetic fact, so both are `DEFINITION` as required. No rule matches execution cells, and no rule is supported by the required “prove first without the rule, then import the exact statement” evidence. Therefore the operational, proved-derived, and domain-lemma sets are all empty for this canonical inventory.
